---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const description = "Control Insidia scan scope, authorize targets, and keep reports on your machine. Learn which services scans contact, how secrets are masked, and how to report issues.";
---
<Base title="Scan Scope, Privacy & Security | Insidia Labs" description={description} path="/security">
  <Header />
  <main id="content" class="wrap" style="padding:3rem 0 4rem">
    <h1>Your app. Your scan scope.</h1>
    <p class="lede">You choose what Insidia may test and where any model requests go. The CLI runs on your machine and saves reports locally.</p>
    <div class="grid-3" style="margin-top:2rem">
      <article class="card">
        <h2>Choose the target</h2>
        <p>Start on localhost. To test a deployed app, list its host in <code>insidia.yaml</code>, set <code>authorized: true</code>, and confirm the scan with <code>--yes</code>. Test only systems you own or have permission to test.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h2>Know where data goes</h2>
        <p>The CLI sends no telemetry. A scan contacts your target and any model endpoint you configure. Detected secrets in finding evidence are masked, for example [AWS_ACCESS_KEY len=20 fp=3f9a1c07].</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h2>Stay in control with an agent</h2>
        <p>The Insidia skill guides your coding agent through the same local workflow. You confirm the hosts before the first scan. The agent reviews the saved findings and opens the report for you.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <section class="block">
      <h2>Get help with security</h2>
      <p>Read the <a href="/docs/start/scope/">scope guide</a> and <a href="/docs/security/data/">data handling guide</a> before configuring a scan. Insidia Cloud is still in development; this website does not run scans or collect your scan reports.</p>
      <p>Found a vulnerability in Insidia itself? Email <a href="mailto:insidialabs@gmail.com?subject=Security%20question">insidialabs@gmail.com</a> so we can investigate privately.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
